<title>UK: Hickson says to reorganise businesses.</title>
<headline>Hickson says to reorganise businesses.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British chemicals group Hickson International Plc said on Monday it planned to reduce the number of operating divisions to two from three, reflecting the recent sale of a number of businesses.  </p>
<p>In a statement, Hickson said it had created a new organic chemicals division which would include its remaining performance chemical operations following the disposal of Hickson Manro in November 1996 and Hickson PharmaChem last month.</p>
<p>The new division will be headed by John Markham.</p>
<p>Mike Fearfield, managing director of the group's defunct performance chemical's arm, has stepped down from the Hickson board and left the company.</p>
<p>Hickson said John Langton would continue to lead the other main division, protection and coatings.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
